ekta A.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Rahbari M","lastName":"Rahbari","firstName":"Mohadese","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of cell and molecular biology-Genetics, University of science and culture, ACECR, Tehran, Iran."}]}},{"fullName":"Lohrasbi R","lastName":"Lohrasbi","firstName":"Reyhane","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Genetics, Reproductive Biomedicine Research Center, Royan Institute for Reproductive BiomedicineACECR, Tehran, Iran."}]}},{"fullName":"Amiri-Yekta A","lastName":"Amiri-Yekta","firstName":"Amir","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8099-7984"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Genetics, Reproductive Biomedicine Research Center, Royan Institute for Reproductive BiomedicineACECR, Tehran, Iran. amir.amiriyekta@royaninstitute.org."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8099-7984"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"301","journalIssueId":4251536,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Sep","monthOfPublication":9,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Mol Genet Genomics","title":"Molecular genetics and genomics : MGG","essn":"1617-4623","issn":"1617-4615","nlmid":"101093320","isoabbreviation":"Mol Genet Genomics"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-09-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"193","abstractText":"Since its introduction as a genome-editing tool, CRISPR-based technology has undergone rapid refinement, with precision emerging as a central focus of development. Early CRISPR-Cas9 systems demonstrated unprecedented ease and efficiency in targeting specific DNA sequences, but concerns over off-target effects and variable editing outcomes limited their broader application. This review outlines the progression of CRISPR from its discovery in prokaryotes to its application as a versatile tool in precision medicine, where it supports targeted therapies for genetic disorders in various ways. Although technical challenges, including off-target editing and delivery inefficiencies, persist alongside ethical considerations of accessibility and long-term consequences, CRISPR's ongoing refinements and innovations reflect a clear trajectory toward greater specificity, safety, and predictability, positioning CRISPR as an increasingly precise platform for both fundamental research and therapeutic use.","affiliation":"Department of cell and molecular biology-Genetics, University of science and culture, ACECR, Tehran, Iran.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Review","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Genetic Therapy","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Precision Medicine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TD","qualifierName":"trends"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Gene therapy","Genome Editing","Crispr/cas","Talen","Zfn","Genome Editing Tools"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00438-026-02467-3"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2026-09-17","dateOfCreation":"2026-09-16","dateOfRevision":"2026-11-05","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-09-17","firstPublicationDate":"2026-09-17","firstIndexDate":"2026-09-17","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"37993945","source":"MED","pmid":"37993945","pmcid":"PMC10664500","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC10664500"]},"doi":"10.1186/s13046-023-02901-z","title":"CRISPR/Cas9: a powerful tool in colorectal cancer research.","authorString":"Hu Y, Liu L, Jiang Q, Fang W, Chen Y, Hong Y, Zhai X.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hu Y","lastName":"Hu","firstName":"Yang","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology, The First People's Hospital of Jiande, Hangzhou, 311600, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu L","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Liang","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Orthopedic Surgery, Zhongnan Hospital of Wuhan University, Wuhan, 430071, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Jiang Q","lastName":"Jiang","firstName":"Qi","initials":"Q","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biological Repositories, Zhongnan Hospital of Wuhan University, Wuhan, 430071, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Fang W","lastName":"Fang","firstName":"Weiping","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology, The First People's Hospital of Jiande, Hangzhou, 311600, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Chen Y","lastName":"Chen","firstName":"Yazhu","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"West China Hospital of Sichuan University, Chengdu, 610044, China. yazhu.chen@qq.com."}]}},{"fullName":"Hong Y","lastName":"Hong","firstName":"Yuntian","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3546-1670"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology, Zhongnan Hospital of Wuhan University, Wuhan, 430071, China. 3130101818@zju.edu.cn."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhai X","lastName":"Zhai","firstName":"Xiang","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Colorectal and Anal Surgery, Zhongnan Hospital of Wuhan University, Wuhan, 430071, China. zx1996@whu.edu.cn."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-3546-1670"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"42","journalIssueId":3656788,"dateOfPublication":"2023 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Exp Clin Cancer Res","title":"Journal of experimental & clinical cancer research : CR","essn":"1756-9966","issn":"0392-9078","nlmid":"8308647","isoabbreviation":"J Exp Clin Cancer Res"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-11-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"308","abstractText":"Colorectal cancer (CRC) is one of the most common malignant cancers worldwide and seriously threatens human health. The clustered regulatory interspaced short palindromic repeat/CRISPR-associate nuclease 9 (CRISPR/Cas9) system is an adaptive immune system of bacteria or archaea. Since its introduction, research into various aspects of treatment approaches for CRC has been accelerated, including investigation of the oncogenes, tumor suppressor genes (TSGs), drug resistance genes, target genes, mouse model construction, and especially in genome-wide library screening. Furthermore, the CRISPR/Cas9 system can be utilized for gene therapy for CRC, specifically involving in the molecular targeted drug delivery or targeted knockout in vivo. In this review, we elucidate the mechanism of the CRISPR/Cas9 system and its comprehensive applications in CRC. Additionally, we discussed the issue of off-target effects associated with CRISPR/Cas9, which serves to restrict its practical application. Future research on CRC should in-depth and systematically utilize the CRISPR/Cas9 system thereby achieving clinical practice.","affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology, The First People's Hospital of Jiande, Hangzhou, 311600, China.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Colorectal Neoplasms","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oncogenes"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Therapy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["target therapy","Crc","Crispr/cas9","Off-target","Precise Medicine","Gene Editing Tool"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13046-023-02901-z"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10664500"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10664500?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":23,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2023-11-24","dateOfCreation":"2023-11-23","dateOfRevision":"2023-11-25","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-11-22","firstPublicationDate":"2023-11-22","firstIndexDate":"2023-11-23","fullTextReceivedDate":"2023-11-24","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"PPR983884","source":"PPR","doi":"10.32942/x2rk8b","title":"Transferable approaches to CRISPR-Cas9 induced genome editing in non-model insects: a brief guide","authorString":"Hunnekuhl V, Ahmed H, Zheng L.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hunnekuhl V","lastName":"Hunnekuhl","firstName":"Vera","initials":"V"},{"fullName":"Ahmed H","lastName":"Ahmed","firstName":"Hassan","initials":"H"},{"fullName":"Zheng L","lastName":"Zheng","firstName":"Lisha","initials":"L"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"pubYear":"2025","abstractText":"Despite the large variety of insect species with divergent morphological, developmental and physiological features questions on gene function could for a long time only be addressed in few model species. The adoption of the bacterial CRISPR-Cas system for genome editing in eukaryotic cells widened the scope of the field of functional genetics: for the first time the creation of heritable genetic changes had become possible in a very broad range of organisms. Since then, targeted genome editing using the CRISPR-Cas technology has greatly increased the possibilities for genetic manipulation in non-model insects where molecular genetic tools were little established. The technology allows for site-specific mutagenesis and germline transformation. Importantly, it can be used for the generation of gene knock-outs, and for the knock-in of transgenes and generation of gene-reporter fusions. CRISPR-Cas induced genome editing can thus be applied to address questions in basic research in various insect species and other study organisms. Notably, it can also be used in applied insect biotechnology to design new pest and vector control strategies such as gene drives and precision guided Sterile Insect Technique. However, establishing CRISPR in a new model requires several practical considerations that depend on the scientific questions and on the characteristics of the respective study organism. Therefore, this review is intended to give a literature overview on different CRISPR-Cas9 based methods that have already been established in diverse insects. After discussing some required pre-conditions of the study organism, we provide a guide through experimental considerations when planning to conduct CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing, such as the design and delivery of guide RNAs, and of Cas9 endonuclease. We discuss the use of different repair mechanisms including homology directed repair (HDR) for a defined insertion of genetic elements. Furthermore, we describe different molecular methods for genetic screening and the use of visible markers. We focus our review on experimental work in insects, but due to the ubiquitous functionality of the CRISPR-Cas system many considerations are transferable to other non-model organisms.","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Preprint"]},"bookOrReportDetails":{"publisher":"EcoEvoRxiv","yearOfPublication":2025},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"doi","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://doi.org/10.32942/x2rk8b"},{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.32942/x2rk8b"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2025-03-11","firstPublicationDate":"2025-02-27","firstIndexDate":"2025-03-12","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"38222734","source":"MED","pmid":"38222734","pmcid":"PMC10783353","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC10783353"]},"doi":"10.1097/ms9.0000000000001500","title":"Application of CRISPR/Cas9 in the management of Alzheimer's disease and Parkinson's disease: a review.","authorString":"Thapar N, Eid MAF, Raj N, Kantas T, Billing HS, Sadhu D.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Thapar N","lastName":"Thapar","firstName":"Nandita","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Manipal College of Medical Sciences, Pokhara, Kaski, Nepal."}]}},{"fullName":"Eid MAF","lastName":"Eid","firstName":"Mosab Ahmad Fathi","initials":"MAF","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Faculty of Medicine and Health Sciences, An-Najah National University, West Bank, Palestine."}]}},{"fullName":"Raj N","lastName":"Raj","firstName":"Nishchita","initials":"N","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Psychiatry, Santosh Medical College and Hospital, Ghaziabad."}]}},{"fullName":"Kantas T","lastName":"Kantas","firstName":"Theodosios","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1418-8118"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Surgery, General State Hospital, Nikaia, Athens, Greece."}]}},{"fullName":"Billing HS","lastName":"Billing","firstName":"Harbir S","initials":"HS","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Government Medical College and Hospital, Chandigarh, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Sadhu D","lastName":"Sadhu","firstName":"Dhavalkumar","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"American University of Barbados School of Medicine, Wildey, Barbados."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1418-8118"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"86","journalIssueId":3696316,"dateOfPublication":"2024 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2024,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Ann Med Surg (Lond)","title":"Annals of medicine and surgery (2012)","essn":"2049-0801","issn":"2049-0801","nlmid":"101616869","isoabbreviation":"Ann Med Surg (Lond)"},"printPublicationDate":"2024-01-01"},"pubYear":"2024","pageInfo":"329-335","abstractText":"The clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats (CRISPR)/CRISPR-associated (Cas) nucleases system (CRISPR/Cas9) is a popular gene-editing technology with an expanding scope in the field of medicine. Recent studies have investigated the role of CRISPR/Cas9 system in the treatment of neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer's disease (AD) and Parkinson's disease (PD). Since the risk of occurrence of both conditions is strongly associated with genetic mutations and variations, the use of gene-editing technologies to rectify these genetic errors becomes relevant. The CRISPR/Cas9 system has been tested in AD, which has led to a decrease in either amyloid beta deposition or tau phosphorylation in cells. Likewise, genetic mutations in cells affected by PD have been corrected with promising results in initial studies undertaken. Therefore, the use of the CRISPR/Cas9 system should be expanded among different populations to understand its efficacy and safety in depth among neurodegenerative conditions.","affiliation":"Manipal College of Medical Sciences, Pokhara, Kaski, Nepal.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic-eCollection","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Alzheimer’s disease","Parkinson’s Disease","Neurodegenerative Disorders","Gene Editing","Crispr/cas9"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"doi","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https