firstName":"Saurabh","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0723-4363"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Pharmaceutics, National Institute of Pharmaceutical Education and Research (NIPER)-Hyderabad, Telangana-500037, Hyderabad, India."}]}},{"fullName":"Vora L","lastName":"Vora","firstName":"Lalitkumar","initials":"L","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8106-9066"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Pharmacy, Queen's University Belfast, 97 Lisburn Road, Belfast, BT9 7BL, UK. L.Vora@qub.ac.uk."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5615-201X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7066-7706"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8106-9066"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0723-4363"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-1792-4894"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"27","journalIssueId":3555628,"dateOfPublication":"2023 May","monthOfPublication":5,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Biomater Res","title":"Biomaterials research","essn":"2055-7124","issn":"1226-4601","nlmid":"101650636","isoabbreviation":"Biomater Res"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-05-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"46","abstractText":"Since its discovery in 2012, CRISPR Cas9 has been tried as a direct treatment approach to correct the causative gene mutation and establish animal models in neurodegenerative disorders. Since no strategy developed until now could completely cure Parkinson's disease (PD), neuroscientists aspire to use gene editing technology, especially CRISPR/Cas9, to induce a permanent correction in genetic PD patients expressing mutated genes. Over the years, our understanding of stem cell biology has improved. Scientists have developed personalized cell therapy using CRISPR/Cas9 to edit embryonic and patient-derived stem cells ex-vivo. This review details the importance of CRISPR/Cas9-based stem cell therapy in Parkinson's disease in developing PD disease models and developing therapeutic strategies after elucidating the possible pathophysiological mechanisms.","affiliation":"Molecular and Cellular Neuroscience Lab, Department of Pharmacology and Toxicology, National Institute of Pharmaceutical Education and Research (NIPER)-Hyderabad, Telangana-500037, Hyderabad, India.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Embryonic stem cells","Disease model","Neurodegenerative disorder","α-synuclein","Human Pluripotent Stem Cells","Gene Editing"]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40824-023-00381-y"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10190035"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10190035?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":39,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["refsnp","nct","doi"]},"dateOfCreation":"2023-05-16","dateOfRevision":"2023-05-19","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-05-16","firstPublicationDate":"2023-05-16","firstIndexDate":"2023-05-18","fullTextReceivedDate":"2025-02-04","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"PPR1346735","source":"PPR","doi":"10.20944/preprints202610.1941.v1","title":"Wine Yeast Engineering for Improved Polysaccharide Depolymerization and Lower Ethyl Carbamate Formation","authorString":"Vasyagin EA, Urakov VN, Shalamitskiy MY, Cherviak SN, Semenova KA, Lutkova NY, Beletsky AV, Rakitin AL, Mardanova ES, Kushnirov VV, Ravin NV, Mardanov AV.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Vasyagin EA","lastName":"Vasyagin","firstName":"Egor","initials":"EA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-2535-1012"}},{"fullName":"Urakov VN","lastName":"Urakov","firstName":"Valery","initials":"VN"},{"fullName":"Shalamitskiy MY","lastName":"Shalamitskiy","firstName":"Maksim Yu.","initials":"MY","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5888-6228"}},{"fullName":"Cherviak SN","lastName":"Cherviak","firstName":"Sofia","initials":"SN"},{"fullName":"Semenova KA","lastName":"Semenova","firstName":"Karina","initials":"KA"},{"fullName":"Lutkova NY","lastName":"Lutkova","firstName":"Natalia Yu.","initials":"NY"},{"fullName":"Beletsky AV","lastName":"Beletsky","firstName":"Alexey","initials":"AV","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7611-2354"}},{"fullName":"Rakitin AL","lastName":"Rakitin","firstName":"Andrey","initials":"AL","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9178-6912"}},{"fullName":"Mardanova ES","lastName":"Mardanova","firstName":"Eugenia","initials":"ES"},{"fullName":"Kushnirov VV","lastName":"Kushnirov","firstName":"Vitaly","initials":"VV","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0316-0766"}},{"fullName":"Ravin NV","lastName":"Ravin","firstName":"Nikolai","initials":"NV","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1456-1832"}},{"fullName":"Mardanov AV","lastName":"Mardanov","firstName":"Andrey","initials":"AV","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8245-8757"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5888-6228"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9551-7448"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1456-1832"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7611-2354"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8245-8757"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9178-6912"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-0316-0766"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2148-7658"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-2535-1012"}]},"pubYear":"2026","abstractText":"Engineering wine yeasts to combine efficient extracellular polysaccharide degradation with reduced accumulation of ethyl carbamate, a group 2A carcinogen, may support improvements in winemaking. This study aimed to replace the arginase-encoding CAR1 locus in the genome of the triploid industrial wine yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae I-328 with an expression cassette for the endopolygalacturonase gene PGU1, placed under the control of the PGK1 gene promoter and terminator. CRISPR/Cas9-mediated genome editing was performed using an acetamidase-selectable plasmid followed by phenotypic screening and molecular genetic verification. Whole genome sequencing confirmed the replacement of all three CAR1 alleles by the PGU1 expression cassettes. The modified strain I328-Y21 showed enhanced degradation of polygalacturonic acid relative to the parental strain. Consistently, RT-qPCR analysis showed that the transcription level of the PGU1 gene in strain I328-Y21 was about 300 times higher than in I-328. Inactivation of arginase, which forms urea through the breakdown of arginine, resulted in about nine-fold decrease in the content of urea in the growth medium. Since ethyl carbamate is formed as a result of the interaction between ethanol and urea excreted by yeast cells, this strain could be used to reduce its content in wine. Winemaking experiments show that genome editing did not affect fermentation performance and other technological characteristics. The new strain with the replacement of the arginase gene with the endopolygalacturonase expression cassette is promising for use in winemaking.","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Preprint"]},"bookOrReportDetails":{"publisher":"Preprints.org","yearOfPublication":2026},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Free","availabilityCode":"F","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202610.1941.v1"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-22","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-20","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-22","versionList":{"version":[{"id":"PPR1346735","source":"PPR","versionNumber":1,"firstPublishDate":"2026-10-20","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["preprint"]},"hasEvaluations":"N"}]},"versionNumber":1,"hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"42081295","source":"MED","pmid":"42081295","doi":"10.1093/procel/pwag030","title":"Human embryo editing: Ten years of breakthroughs and challenges.","authorString":"Zhou Y, Xie D, Ding C, Wu W, Cao T, Liu Q, Keefe DL, Zhou C, Huang J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Zhou Y","lastName":"Zhou","firstName":"Yitong","initials":"Y","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Xie D","lastName":"Xie","firstName":"Dongchun","initials":"D","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Ding C","lastName":"Ding","firstName":"Chenhui","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, Reproductive Medical Center, The First Affiliated Hospital, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wu W","lastName":"Wu","firstName":"Wenlian","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Cao T","lastName":"Cao","firstName":"Tianqi","initials":"T","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Liu Q","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Qianyi","initials":"Q","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Keefe DL","lastName":"Keefe","firstName":"David L","initials":"DL","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, NYU Langone Fertility Center, NYU Langone, New York, NY, 10016, United States."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhou C","lastName":"Zhou","firstName":"Canquan","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, Reproductive Medical Center, The First Affiliated Hospital, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Huang J","lastName":"Huang","firstName":"Junjiu","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China."},{"affiliation":"Guangdong Provincial Key Laboratory of Reproductive Medicine, The First Affiliated Hospital and School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510080, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6798-9552"}]},"journalInfo":{"journalIssueId":4189434,"dateOfPublication":"2026 May","monthOfPublication":5,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Protein Cell","title":"Protein & cell","essn":"1674-8018","issn":"1674-800X","nlmid":"101532368","isoabbreviation":"Protein Cell"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-05-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"pwag030","abstractText":"Over the past decade, the field of human embryo editing has witnessed remarkable advancements and triggered significant ethical debates. The groundbreaking tool, CRISPR/Cas9, has revolutionized the landscape of genetic engineering by enabling modifications at the genomic level in germ cells. Since the first case of human embryo gene editing in 2015, the field has rapidly progressed, presenting promising avenues for therapeutic interventions. However, it still grapples with safety concerns, including off-target effects, mosaicism, and the long-term impacts of genetic alterations, as well as ongoing ethical controversies. In this review, we will systematically overview the significant research in this field and provide insights into the potential applications of basic research in early embryonic development and the treatment of genetic diseases.","affiliation":"MOE Key Laboratory of Gene Function and Regulation, State Key Laboratory of Biocontrol, School of Life Sciences, Sun Yat-sen University, Guangzhou, 510275, China.","publicationStatus":"aheadofprint","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Key Research and Development Program of China","grantId":"2025YFA1309500","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"82271688","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"32570938","orderIn":0}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/procel/pwag030"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-05-04","dateOfRevision":"2026-05-04","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-05-03","firstPublicationDate":"2026-05-03","firstIndexDate":"2026-05-13","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"39387692","source":"MED","pmid":"39387692","pmcid":"PMC11714751","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC11714751"]},"doi":"10.1093/jxb/erae424","title":"CRISPR/Cas9 editing of two adenine phosphoribosyl transferase coding genes reveals the functional specialization of adenine salvage proteins in common bean.","authorString":"López CM, Alseekh S, Martínez Rivas FJ, Fernie AR, Prieto P, Alamillo JM.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"López CM","lastName":"López","firstName":"Cristina Mª","initi