aka A, Tomatsu S.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Leal AF","lastName":"Leal","firstName":"Andrés Felipe","initials":"AF","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5956-1986"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA."},{"affiliation":"Institute for the Study of Inborn Errors of Metabolism, Faculty of Science, Pontificia Universidad Javeriana, Bogotá 110231, Colombia."}]}},{"fullName":"Herreno-Pachón AM","lastName":"Herreno-Pachón","firstName":"Angelica María","initials":"AM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA."},{"affiliation":"Faculty of Arts and Sciences, University of Delaware, Newark, DE 19716, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Benincore-Flórez E","lastName":"Benincore-Flórez","firstName":"Eliana","initials":"E","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9791-2716"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Karunathilaka A","lastName":"Karunathilaka","firstName":"Amali","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA."},{"affiliation":"Faculty of Arts and Sciences, University of Delaware, Newark, DE 19716, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Tomatsu S","lastName":"Tomatsu","firstName":"Shunji","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0673-2160"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA."},{"affiliation":"Faculty of Arts and Sciences, University of Delaware, Newark, DE 19716, USA."},{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Graduate School of Medicine, Gifu University, Gifu 501-1194, Japan."},{"affiliation":"Department of Pediatrics, Thomas Jefferson University, Philadelphia, PA 19144, USA."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5956-1986"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9791-2716"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0673-2160"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"5","volume":"25","journalIssueId":3738931,"dateOfPublication":"2024 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2024,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Int J Mol Sci","title":"International journal of molecular sciences","essn":"1422-0067","issn":"1422-0067","nlmid":"101092791","isoabbreviation":"Int J Mol Sci"},"printPublicationDate":"2024-02-01"},"pubYear":"2024","pageInfo":"2456","abstractText":"Since its discovery in 2012, the clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats (CRISPR) and CRISPR-associated protein 9 (Cas9) system has supposed a promising panorama for developing novel and highly precise genome editing-based gene therapy (GT) alternatives, leading to overcoming the challenges associated with classical GT. Classical GT aims to deliver transgenes to the cells via their random integration in the genome or episomal persistence into the nucleus through lentivirus (LV) or adeno-associated virus (AAV), respectively. Although high transgene expression efficiency is achieved by using either LV or AAV, their nature can result in severe side effects in humans. For instance, an LV (NCT03852498)- and AAV9 (NCT05514249)-based GT clinical trials for treating X-linked adrenoleukodystrophy and Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy showed the development of myelodysplastic syndrome and patient's death, respectively. In contrast with classical GT, the CRISPR/Cas9-based genome editing requires the homologous direct repair (HDR) machinery of the cells for inserting the transgene in specific regions of the genome. This sophisticated and well-regulated process is limited in the cell cycle of mammalian cells, and in turn, the nonhomologous end-joining (NHEJ) predominates. Consequently, seeking approaches to increase HDR efficiency over NHEJ is crucial. This manuscript comprehensively reviews the current alternatives for improving the HDR for CRISPR/Cas9-based GTs.","affiliation":"Nemours Children's Health, Wilmington, DE 19803, USA.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"The Bennett Foundation","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"The Vain and Harry Fish Foundation, Inc.","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"A Cure for Robert, Inc.","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Austrian MPS society","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"The Carol Ann Foundation","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NICHD NIH HHS","acronym":"HD","grantId":"R01 HD102545","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Jacob Randall Foundation","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institute of Child Health and Human Development of the National Institutes of Health (NICHD)","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Eunice Kennedy Shriver","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Nemours Funds","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Angelo R. Cali and Mary V. Cali Family Foundation, Inc.","grantId":"1R01HD102545-01A1","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mammals","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"DNA End-Joining Repair"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Recombinational DNA Repair"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Therapy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Editing"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Nhej","Hdr","Genome Editing","Crispr/cas9"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/1422-0067/25/5/2456/pdf?version=1708402935"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms25052456"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10931195"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10931195?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":44,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["nct","doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2024-03-14","dateOfCreation":"2024-03-13","dateOfRevision":"2024-03-16","electronicPublicationDate":"2024-02-20","firstPublicationDate":"2024-02-20","firstIndexDate":"2024-03-13","fullTextReceivedDate":"2024-03-15","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"38136570","source":"MED","pmid":"38136570","pmcid":"PMC10741458","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC10741458"]},"doi":"10.3390/biom13121698","title":"gRNA Design: How Its Evolution Impacted on CRISPR/Cas9 Systems Refinement.","authorString":"Motoche-Monar C, Ordoñez JE, Chang O, Gonzales-Zubiate FA.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Motoche-Monar C","lastName":"Motoche-Monar","firstName":"Cristofer","initials":"C","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0819-5848"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Biological Sciences and Engineering, Yachay Tech University, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador."}]}},{"fullName":"Ordoñez JE","lastName":"Ordoñez","firstName":"Julián E","initials":"JE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0004-2313-8173"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Biological Sciences and Engineering, Yachay Tech University, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador."}]}},{"fullName":"Chang O","lastName":"Chang","firstName":"Oscar","initials":"O","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4336-7545"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Departamento de Electrónica, Universidad Simon Bolivar, Caracas 1080, Venezuela."},{"affiliation":"MIND Research Group, Model Intelligent Networks Development, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador."}]}},{"fullName":"Gonzales-Zubiate FA","lastName":"Gonzales-Zubiate","firstName":"Fernando A","initials":"FA","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9519-4079"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Biological Sciences and Engineering, Yachay Tech University, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador."},{"affiliation":"MIND Research Group, Model Intelligent Networks Development, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9519-4079"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0819-5848"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4336-7545"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0004-2313-8173"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"13","journalIssueId":3685375,"dateOfPublication":"2023 Nov","monthOfPublication":11,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Biomolecules","title":"Biomolecules","essn":"2218-273X","issn":"2218-273X","nlmid":"101596414","isoabbreviation":"Biomolecules"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-11-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"1698","abstractText":"Over the past decade, genetic engineering has witnessed a revolution with the emergence of a relatively new genetic editing tool based on RNA-guided nucleases: the CRISPR/Cas9 system. Since the first report in 1987 and characterization in 2007 as a bacterial defense mechanism, this system has garnered immense interest and research attention. CRISPR systems provide immunity to bacteria against invading genetic material; however, with specific modifications in sequence and structure, it becomes a precise editing system capable of modifying the genomes of a wide range of organisms. The refinement of these modifications encompasses diverse approaches, including the development of more accurate nucleases, understanding of the cellular context and epigenetic conditions, and the re-designing guide RNAs (gRNAs). Considering the critical importance of the correct performance of CRISPR/Cas9 systems, our scope will emphasize the latter approach. Hence, we present an overview of the past and the most recent guide RNA web-based design tools, highlighting the evolution of their computational architecture and gRNA characteristics over the years. Our study explains computational approaches that use machine learning techniques, neural networks, and gRNA/target interactions data to enable predictions and classifications. This review could open the door to a dynamic community that uses up-to-date algorithms to optimize and create promising gRNAs, suitable for modern CRISPR/Cas9 engineering.","affiliation":"School of Biological Sciences and Engineering, Yachay Tech University, Urcuquí 100119, Ecuador.","publicationStatus":"epublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["review-article","Review","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Algorithms"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"CRISPR-Cas Systems","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Machine Learning"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Editing","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"MT","qualifierName":"methods"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"RNA, Guide, CRISPR-Cas Systems"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Neural networks","Machine Learning","Crispr/cas9","Grna","Deep Learning"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"RNA, Guide, CRISPR-Cas Systems","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Unpaywall","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/2218-273X/13/12/1698/pdf?version=1700797616"},{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biom13121698"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10741458"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC10741458?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"PPR","id":"PPR646758","type":"Preprint in","note":"CrossRef Pre-print loader","orderIn":10002}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":6,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2023-12-25","dateOfCreation":"2023-12-23","dateOfRevision":"2024-01-04","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-11-24","firstPublicationDate":"2023-11-24","firstIndexDate":"2023-12-24","fullTextReceivedDate":"2024-01-03","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}